From e992b0a729d8dcb0e94e4ad32293056b5559c65c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:22:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(multiaxis): Rotary Flow kernel - flow lines between
 picked helical guide chains

The first slice of #2804 (issue #2824): a 4-axis cylindrical
flow-line finishing kernel in `multiaxis::rotary_flow`. The caller
picks the guide chains and states the rotation axis (the #2772
seam - the axis is a parameter, never fitted here).

- `rotary_flow_unwrap.rs`: each chain unwound to a continuous
  (theta, v) track about the stated axis (the radian twin of
  `cl::unwrap_near`), each adjacent pair aligned by the nearest
  whole turn, the band developed `(s = R_ref * theta, v)` and its
  cross width read at matched arc length.
- `rotary_flow_pass.rs`: iso-parametric flow curves between the
  aligned pair, each station's ball center pushed out along its
  radial until the `closest_pt_tri` oracle clears every facet, the
  curve chorded within min(ARC_FIT_TOL, tolerance) over the union
  of the two chains' arc-length knots.
- `rotary_flow_emit.rs`: tips via the pivot law, cut poses through
  the lean law on the radial, links rebuilt radially on the retract
  cylinders (`rotary_links`' law), the program opening on the
  clearance pose (M13.8).

Refused by name: a tool that is not a ball-nose, fewer than two
chains, a non-finite or off-model chain point, a chain point on
the axis line, chains wound in opposite senses, a band with no
width, a stepover or tolerance at the scallop ceiling, a station
the push-out cannot clear, a pass count over the ceiling, a
clearance that does not clear the work.

The decisions taken unattended are recorded in
`docs/decisions/2824-rotary-flow-kernel.md`.

Refs #2824
